  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "So the AITER per-tensor quant kernel doesn't support MI300 & MI325? In what way does the test fail exactly?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-20T20:04:52Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/62733#issuecomment-6300312119",
      "id": 6300312119,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-20T20:04:52Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "micah-wil"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "> So the AITER per-tensor quant kernel doesn't support MI300 & MI325? In what way does the test fail exactly?\r\n\r\nAiter uses the full fp8fnuz range of [-240,240], whereas vLLM uses an adjusted range of [-224,224], presumably for accuracy reasons.\r\n\r\nThe test fails when, for instance, a clamp on the expected value saturates to 224, but on the actual value saturates to 240.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-20T21:18:21Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/62733#issuecomment-6301698960",
      "id": 6301698960,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-20T21:18:21Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "rjrock"
      }
    }
